The brief has some internal inconsistencies. It says Israel qualified comfortably from the first semi-final, yet the cutoff is May 9 and the semi-finals had not yet happened. It also says Israel is a "Big 5" automatic finalist, which is wrong. I therefore treat those claims as unreliable.

The most useful figure is the betting-implied probability. It started at about 9% in February and fell to roughly 1.5–2% by May 9, though some markets may have put it higher. The brief also describes strong competition and an EBU crackdown on coordinated voting. I settle on a probability near the market figure, about 3%, to allow for uncertainty in the brief.


