The brief gives an implied probability of about 1.5-2% in some betting markets as of May 9, 2026, down from 9% in February. The brief has an inconsistency: it says Israel "qualified comfortably" from the first semi-final, but the semi-finals had not yet been held by May 9. It also says Israel is a "Big 5" automatic finalist, which is wrong, so the brief is partly unreliable.

Other bookmaker figures in the brief ran from 9% to 20%. Those are older, and the latest figure is much lower. I'll put the probability at roughly 4%, above the quoted 1.5-2% market figure because of the brief's unreliability and Israel's strong televote history.


